<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phetracha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1632–1703</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phetracha was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> from 1688 to 1703 and founder of the Ban Phlu Luang dynasty. Commander of the royal elephant corps under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narai">Narai</a>, he seized power as Narai lay dying in 1688, executed the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-phaulkon">Constantine Phaulkon</a> and forced the French garrison to leave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>, ending the period of close ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phetracha.jpg" alt="Phetracha" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gaspar Bouttats, (sr.) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PITERA_TJAY_Rex_Siam_by_Gaspar_Bouttat_1690.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
